{# The "ordre" question as the student answers it: one row per proposition, ranked either with the
   two arrows or by dragging the row. Shared by the three screens that let a student answer -
   the attempt (program/quiz_question), the video cue overlay (student/_video_cue_question) and
   the library's own test run (library/quiz_test) - because the markup is what the controller
   binds to, and three copies would drift.

   The submitted rank is the *position* of the hidden input in the form, never a separate rank
   field the client and the server could contradict: App\Controller\ProgramQuizAttemptController
   and App\Service\QuizAttemptGrader read the submission order of answers[].

   field_name is the only thing that differs between callers (the test run answers several
   questions in one form, so it indexes by question). #}
<div class="cm-answers cm-order" data-controller="quiz-reorder">
    {% for answer in answers %}
        <div class="cm-answer-row cm-order__row" draggable="true"
             data-quiz-reorder-target="row"
             data-action="dragstart->quiz-reorder#dragStart dragover->quiz-reorder#dragOver drop->quiz-reorder#drop dragend->quiz-reorder#dragEnd">
            <span class="cm-qbank__index" data-quiz-reorder-target="rank">{{ loop.index }}</span>
            <span class="cm-answer-input" style="cursor:inherit;">{{ answer.label }}</span>
            <input type="hidden" name="{{ field_name }}" value="{{ answer.id }}" data-quiz-reorder-target="input">
            <button type="button" class="cm-answer-move" data-action="click->quiz-reorder#moveUp" aria-label="{{ 'moveUpActionLabel'|trans }}">▲</button>
            <button type="button" class="cm-answer-move" data-action="click->quiz-reorder#moveDown" aria-label="{{ 'moveDownActionLabel'|trans }}">▼</button>
            <span class="cm-order__handle" aria-hidden="true">⋮⋮</span>
        </div>
    {% endfor %}
</div>
